course: dictionary
lesson: 15525
title: Below the surface
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from parts that give clues. Sub means under, and surface means the top layer of something. Put them together and subsurface means just below the top.
explain: Ruby reads, «The drill found subsurface water beneath the field.» The water is under the soil, not on top, so subsurface must mean lying below the surface. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The drill found water lying just below the surface» still makes sense.
explain: Scientists write about «a subsurface ocean» on the moon Europa. They cannot see it directly, but they think there is water hidden under the icy top layer.
fact: Subsurface means lying or happening just below a surface.
fact: The subsurface is the layer under the surface, such as under the ground, the sea or the skin.
fact: «Subsurface water» means groundwater under the soil.
fact: Scientists look for «subsurface oceans» on moons like Europa and Enceladus.
fact: Engineers do subsurface surveys to check the ground before they build.
exercise: «The drill found subsurface water beneath the field.» What does subsurface mean here? | *Lying just below the ground | Floating high in the sky | Splashing over the top | Very cold and frozen
exercise: Engineers do a subsurface survey before building. What do they check? | The height of the trees | *The ground under the surface | The names of the workers | The colour of the paint
exercise: Which word means lying just below a surface? | airborne | summit | skyline | *subsurface
test: «Scientists think a subsurface ocean may be hidden under the icy top of Europa.» What does subsurface mean here? | Far away in space | *Hidden just beneath the surface | Very salty and warm | Frozen solid at the very top
test: Which of these is a subsurface layer? | The leaves on a tree | *Fat and muscle just under the skin | The rainbow above the hill | A cloud high in the sky
exam: Sam reads, «The subsurface was dry, but the rain soaked through the top soil.» What is the best meaning of subsurface? | Wet and full of rain | The highest point of a hill | *The layer lying beneath the top of the ground | A type of rain cloud
